In [ 39 ], a method for approximate estimation of shear deformation based on analysis of grain misorientation angle distribution was proposed. The method is based on the assumption that during the stage of intensive grain refinement under simple shear deformation, the shape of the misorientation angle distribution is uniquely determined by the amount of deformation. Work [ 39 ] presents distribution diagrams for ten different values of shear deformation in the range from 2 to 24. It is shown in [ 39 ] that at for a shear deformation of magnitude  γ  ≈ 20, the distribution shape approaches a statistically random form described by the Mackenzie curve. Subsequent progress in deformation does not alter the distribution shape. Comparison of the obtained distribution with the reference curves from [ 39 ] allows an approximate estimate of the deformation level in the studied areas. In the process of simple shear, the following expression for the effective strain is obtained from formula ( 2 ) (cf. also [ 40 ]): 4 e eff = γ 3 \documentclass[12pt]{minimal}
